✅ 5. What is hoisting in JavaScript?
Hoisting is JavaScript’s behavior of moving declarations to the top of the current scope (function or global).
console.log(a); // undefined
var a = 5;

✅ 6. Explain the concept of “undefined” vs. “null”.
undefined: A variable declared but not assigned any value.
null: A variable that is clearly set to no value.
let x;
console.log(x); // undefined

let y = null;
console.log(y); // null

